  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supportive activities for the purpose of combi-track Life Science and Health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will enable the Netherlands embassy in Nairobi, Kenya to support with activities on the further development of the combi-track on healthcare, when needed. The activities will be focussed on bringing stakeholders together whenever needed in support of a well-balanced combi-track.This combi-track is part of the Multi-Annual Country Strategy (MACS) of the Netherlands embassy in Nairobi, Kenya.The Life Science and Health (LSH) sector is an important driver for economic development and the combi-track builds on the long-standing support of the Netherlands to Kenya&apos;s health ambitions. The challenge of the combi-track is to support the transition of the Kenya health sector and involve the private sector (Kenyan and Dutch) in this transition.The Kenyan Ministry of Health recognises that well-structured collaboration with the private sector can deliver additional value and help achieve health-related goals, including Universal Health Coverage.</narrative>
  </description>
